{#
  partials/persona-card.njk — one persona in a .profile-grid

  Usage: set `cardPersona` before including.
    {% set cardPersona = persona %}
    {% include "partials/persona-card.njk" %}

  A thin wrapper over partials/tile.njk, the same tile the named IT workers
  render through, so the two listings are one design rather than two that nearly
  match. A persona puts its mirrored avatar in the picture slot, its name on the
  line below, and LIVE beside that name where it still holds a live account.

  What is deliberately NOT on the card: the alias chips, the indicator counts and
  the account headline it used to carry. A persona can be reported under a dozen
  names, and six tiles across a row they swamped the name a reader is scanning
  for. All of it is on the persona's own page.

  cardPersona.avatar is hoisted onto the persona in scripts/lib/personas.js,
  because the listing sorts on it as well as rendering it. It is either the
  avatar a LinkedIn account presents or a mirrored photograph a researcher or
  registry published. Neither is evidence of who runs the account: an avatar is
  routinely stock imagery or a picture taken from an uninvolved person, and a
  published photograph shows whoever appeared under the identity, not
  necessarily whoever it was built from. That is why it is decorative here with
  an empty alt, and carries its caveat in full on the persona's own page.

  The text the listing's search box matches against, read by
  src/assets/js/persona-filter.js, goes in `data-search`. It deliberately reaches
  past the card into the persona's own indicators, because the useful search on
  this page is an identifier rather than a name: pasting an address or a GitHub
  handle should land on the persona holding it. Renaming data-search means
  changing that script too.
#}
{% set cardSearch = [cardPersona.name, cardPersona.slug, cardPersona.heading] %}
{% for alias in cardPersona.aliases %}{% set cardSearch = (cardSearch.push(alias), cardSearch) %}{% endfor %}
{% for account in cardPersona.accounts %}{% set cardSearch = (cardSearch.push(account.handle + " " + account.url), cardSearch) %}{% endfor %}
{% for identifier in cardPersona.identifiers %}{% set cardSearch = (cardSearch.push(identifier.value), cardSearch) %}{% endfor %}
{% if cardPersona.accounts[0].status and cardPersona.accounts[0].status.profile %}
  {% set searchProfile = cardPersona.accounts[0].status.profile %}
  {# Each of these three is optional on a profile record -- a LinkedIn account
     can display a location and no headline at all -- and Nunjucks renders a
     missing one as the literal string "undefined", which lands in data-search
     and trips check-site's template-leak rule. Default them to empty. #}
  {% set cardSearch = (cardSearch.push((searchProfile.headline | default("")) + " " + (searchProfile.location | default("")) + " " + (searchProfile.current_role | default(""))), cardSearch) %}
{% endif %}
{%- set tile = {
  href: "/remote-workers/personas/" + cardPersona.slug + "/",
  photo: cardPersona.avatar,
  empty: "No photograph",
  name: cardPersona.name if cardPersona.name else (cardPersona.accounts[0].handle if cardPersona.accounts.length else cardPersona.slug),
  badge: "LIVE" if cardPersona.live_accounts else null,
  attrs: 'data-search="' + (cardSearch | join(" ") | lower | escape) + '"'
} -%}
{% include "partials/tile.njk" %}
